---
code: K0040
title: Function is missing return type
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: false
---

Function declarations in Kura require an explicit return type annotation before the [`=>`]{.expected} arrow.

Example of erroneous code:

```kura
fn counter-buttons() =>
  #row() {
    #button(:inc, on-click: Increment) { #text("+") }
  }
```

Add `: ReturnType` after the parameter list (for example, `Element` for UI view functions or `()` when returning nothing):

```kura
fn counter-buttons(): Node =>
  #row() {
    #button(:inc, on-click: Increment) { #text("+") }
  }
```

::: note
Explicit return types allow the Kura compiler to verify layout and reactivity contracts ahead of time without whole-program type inference.
:::
